# Verify and hand off a working app

**Full procedure:** [`.cursor/skills/agent-ui/SKILL.md`](../skills/agent-ui/SKILL.md).

After app-affecting Expo changes, prove the surface on **both** iOS (`onTrack iPhone 17 Pro`, latest iOS runtime) and Android (Galaxy_S26). **Default close-out** (`verify-both` runs platforms in parallel):

```bash
# Already on route → omit --flow; otherwise pass a named flow (travel-demo, …)
./scripts/agent-ui-verify-both.sh --route <path> [--flow <name>] --exists <id> …
```

Paste both assert outputs. One verify-both per close-out — don’t grind retries / `SKIP_LEASE`. Exceptions: pure docs/rules, host-only scripts, or user scoped one platform.

- Prefer named `--flow` / seeds over hand-built `--goto` / `--wait` chains.
- Pin `AGENT_UI_PLATFORM=android` for Android; clear before iOS (sticky pin breaks default). `verify-both` does this.
- **Headless agent devices only** — one dedicated slot per agent (`onTrack Agent N` / `onTrack_Agent_N`, **max 2 per platform**). No free slot → exit 3, report the skip, stop without testing; never wait and never fall back to the user's `onTrack iPhone 17 Pro` / `Galaxy_S26`. Launches over 30s are a defect to diagnose. Do not set `ONTRACK_IOS_SIMULATOR_WINDOW=1` or run `ensure-android-emulator.sh --window` / `android:ensure:window` unless the user explicitly asks for a headed Simulator/AVD.
- **Own account per device** — `./scripts/agent-ui.sh login` signs the leased device into its `agent_N` account (dev-only, `account_flags.agent_test` required); `--guest` stays credential-free.
- Reuse Metro when healthy; agents use `packager:ensure:start` — never `npm start` in agent shells. No prophylactic force-stop / `--force-reconnect`.
- Assert/`--color` then **STOP** — no ritual handoff screenshot. Glyph orientation → source, not screenshots.
- Leave devices on the changed surface (not splash/blank/error/unrelated tab).
- Verify slow or flaky after a retry or two → fix the blocker ([`stuck-check-config.mdc`](./stuck-check-config.mdc)); do not loop retries.
